# PREIshare environment variables: TEMPLATE ONLY
#
# Names only. NEVER put a real key, password, or URL in this file: it is committed to git.
# To use it: copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in values there. On Vercel, set them in
# Project Settings → Environment Variables instead.
#
# Requirements:  docs/requirements/sponsor-auth-and-listings-brief.md (section 8, server-only boundary)
# Setup steps:   docs/setup/supabase-env-checklist.md
#
# Status: sign-in (/login) and the /dashboard guard read these variables. With them empty,
# nobody can sign in and /dashboard redirects to /login. Fill them in a local .env once the
# Supabase project exists and the migrations in supabase/migrations/ are applied.
#
# Labels:
#   PUBLIC       → `VITE_` prefix. Copied into the browser bundle; anyone can read it. Never a secret.
#   SERVER-ONLY  → no `VITE_` prefix. Read with `process.env.NAME` inside a server function handler
#                  (createServerFn / createServerOnlyFn / a *.server.ts file), never at the top of a file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-ONLY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SERVER-ONLY (not secret). Supabase project URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
SUPABASE_URL=

# SERVER-ONLY (public-safe key, kept on the server by our design).
# Supabase "anon" or "publishable" key. Used by server functions acting as the signed-in user,
# so Row Level Security still applies.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# SERVER-ONLY: SECRET. Supabase "service_role" or "secret" key. BYPASSES ALL Row Level Security.
# Admin/maintenance jobs only. Never prefix with VITE_, never log it, never commit it.
# If it is ever exposed, rotate it in the Supabase dashboard immediately.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# SERVER-ONLY: SECRET (optional). Direct Postgres connection string, contains the database password.
# Only needed if a tool (e.g. running migrations) connects to Postgres directly.
# DATABASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLIC (client-safe): browser sign-in / sign-out
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used by src/lib/supabase/client.ts for sign-in and sign-out in the browser (login template).
# Safe to expose because Row Level Security is enabled on every table
# (supabase/migrations/). Same project URL and anon key as the server-only pair above.

# PUBLIC. Supabase project URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# PUBLIC. Supabase "anon" or "publishable" key. Every request made with it is checked by RLS.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
#
# FORBIDDEN, never create: VITE_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, VITE_DATABASE_URL, or any VITE_ secret.
